= Deployment Guide
Jane Doe <jane@example.com>
v2.1, 2026-10-01
:toc: left
:icons: font
:source-highlighter: rouge
:project-name: Orbit
:!sectnums:
:description: A service that keeps orbits stable \
  and predictable.

[[intro]]
== Introduction

Welcome to {project-name}. This guide explains how to install, configure and
operate the service. See <<configuration>> or xref:faq.adoc#limits[the FAQ] for details.
Words can be **strongly** bold, __constrained__ italic, `monospace`, ``mono``spaced,
#highlighted#, ##partly##marked, H~2~O and E=mc^2^.
"`Smart quotes`" and '`single smart quotes`' render typographically.
Press kbd:[Ctrl+Shift+P] and choose menu:View[Command Palette > Reload].
A trademark(TM), an ellipsis... and an arrow -> look nice. &copy; &#169;
The value is pass:[<u>raw HTML</u>] and +++<b>passthrough</b>+++ text.
Inline math: stem:[sqrt(4) = 2] and latexmath:[\alpha + \beta].
This sentence needs a footnote.footnote:disclaimer[Use at your own risk.] +
Visit https://example.com[the website], link:docs/index.html[local docs] or mailto:support@example.com[support].
That line ends with a hard break.

=== Requirements

NOTE: The service requires Java 21 or newer.

WARNING: Never expose the admin port to the internet.

[IMPORTANT]
====
Back up your database before upgrading.
====

. Install the package
. Create a configuration file
.. Copy the example
.. Edit the values
. Start the service

